<title>FRANCE: ADP export traffic down 0.8 percent in August.</title>
<headline>ADP export traffic down 0.8 percent in August.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>August 1996 export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 47,063 tonnes, a decrease of 0.8 percent on the same month last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Traffic on the ADP's major export route, North America, fell by two percent on August 1995 to 13,000 tonnes while shipments to the Far East declined by 6.7 percent to 9,807 tonnes.</p>
<p>In contrast, shipments from CDG and Orly to the European Union rose by 14.0 percent to 5,402 tonnes with exports to the Middle East increased by rose by 5.8 percent to 4,790 tonnes.</p>
<p>The ADP's global export traffic in August 1996, by region, with percentage change on August 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		  4,124 tonnes    up    4.6pct</p>
<p> European Union	  5,402 tonnes    up   14.0</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	     973 tonnes    down 16.3</p>
<p> North Africa		868 tonnes    down  5.9</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    3,785 tonnes    up    5.4</p>
<p> North America	  13,000 tonnes    down  2.0</p>
<p> French territories    1,930 tonnes    down 18.7</p>
<p> Latin America	   2,384  tonnes   down  0.5</p>
<p> Middle East	     4,790  tonnes   up    5.8</p>
<p> Far East		  9,807  tonnes   down  6.7</p>
<p> Total		    47,063 tonnes    down  0.8</p>
